<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VII </span><span id="S7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Appendix</span></h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix presents the proofs and experimental details underlying the results reported in the main text.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S7.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">VII-A</span> </span><span id="S7.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 ‣ III-B The Proposed Closed-Loop System ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To achieve the closed-form solution of the QP problem (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), we consider the following Lagrangian associated with (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>):</p>
<table id="S7.Ex19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex19X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\boldsymbol{a},c,\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2})=\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{a}^{\prime}\boldsymbol{a}+\frac{w}{2}c^{2}-\lambda_{1}\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{a},c)-\lambda_{2}c," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\boldsymbol{a},c,\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2})=\frac{1}{2}\boldsymbol{a}^{\prime}\boldsymbol{a}+\frac{w}{2}c^{2}-\lambda_{1}\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{a},c)-\lambda_{2}c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> are Lagrange multipliers of function <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{a},c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(\boldsymbol{a},c)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. By following the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) condition, the following holds:</p>
<table id="S7.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\boldsymbol{a}}=\boldsymbol{a}^{\prime}-\lambda_{1}L_{g}=\mathbf{0}_{p},\\
\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial c}=wc-\lambda_{1}\frac{\partial\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)}{\partial c}-\lambda_{2}=0,\\
-\lambda_{1}(L_{f}+L_{g}\boldsymbol{a}+\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)=0,\\
-\lambda_{2}c=0,\quad\lambda_{1}\geq 0,\quad\lambda_{2}\geq 0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\boldsymbol{a}}=\boldsymbol{a}^{\prime}-\lambda_{1}L_{g}=\mathbf{0}_{p},\\
\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial c}=wc-\lambda_{1}\frac{\partial\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)}{\partial c}-\lambda_{2}=0,\\
-\lambda_{1}(L_{f}+L_{g}\boldsymbol{a}+\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)=0,\\
-\lambda_{2}c=0,\quad\lambda_{1}\geq 0,\quad\lambda_{2}\geq 0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{a}=L_{f}+\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}(G(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{G}^{*})-G(\boldsymbol{\theta}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{a}=L_{f}+\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}(G(\boldsymbol{\theta}_{G}^{*})-G(\boldsymbol{\theta}))</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)=\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)=\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the closed-form solution of (<a href="#S7.E30" title="In VII-A Proof of Lemma ‣ VII Appendix ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) is:</p>
<table id="S7.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\text{if}\ \lambda_{1}=0,\lambda_{2}\geq 0,\quad&amp;\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbf{0}_{p},\ c^{*}=0,\\
\text{if}\ \lambda_{1}&gt;0,\lambda_{2}=0,\quad&amp;\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{-L_{a}L_{g}^{\prime}}{L_{g}L_{g}^{\prime}+\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}^{2}/w},c^{*}=\frac{-\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}L_{a}}{wL_{g}L_{g}^{\prime}+\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}^{2}},\\
\text{if}\ \lambda_{1}&gt;0,\lambda_{2}&gt;0,\quad&amp;\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{-L_{a}L_{g}^{\prime}}{L_{g}L_{g}^{\prime}},c^{*}=0.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>if</mtext><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\text{if}\ \lambda_{1}=0,\lambda_{2}\geq 0,\quad&amp;\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbf{0}_{p},\ c^{*}=0,\\
\text{if}\ \lambda_{1}&gt;0,\lambda_{2}=0,\quad&amp;\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{-L_{a}L_{g}^{\prime}}{L_{g}L_{g}^{\prime}+\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}^{2}/w},c^{*}=\frac{-\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}L_{a}}{wL_{g}L_{g}^{\prime}+\gamma_{\mathrm{h}}^{2}},\\
\text{if}\ \lambda_{1}&gt;0,\lambda_{2}&gt;0,\quad&amp;\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{-L_{a}L_{g}^{\prime}}{L_{g}L_{g}^{\prime}},c^{*}=0.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="S7.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S7.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">VII-B</span> </span><span id="S7.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 ‣ III-C Analysis ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because the closed-loop controller <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> to the nominal gradient descent update is not bounded and can take any necessary magnitude and direction, it is sufficient to show that when <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{g}\equiv\mathbf{0}_{p}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{g}\equiv\mathbf{0}_{p}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the CBF inequality constraint <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}+\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}+\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> holds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. Following the parameter dynamics in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall c\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall c\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding Lie derivatives are given by:</p>
<table id="S7.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S7.EGx2" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.E31.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.E31.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.E31.1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}h(\boldsymbol{\theta})^{\prime}\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}J(\boldsymbol{\theta})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}h(\boldsymbol{\theta})^{\prime}\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}J(\boldsymbol{\theta}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.E31.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.E31.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.E31.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}h(\boldsymbol{\theta})^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}h(\boldsymbol{\theta})^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Clearly, (<a href="#S7.E31.2" title="In 31 ‣ VII-B Proof of Lemma ‣ VII Appendix ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31b</span></a>) can only be nullified if <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}h(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbf{0}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}h(\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbf{0}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which would also nullify (<a href="#S7.E31.1" title="In 31 ‣ VII-B Proof of Lemma ‣ VII Appendix ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31a</span></a>). Therefore, when <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{g}=\mathbf{0}_{p}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{g}=\mathbf{0}_{p}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{f}+\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{f}+\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which always holds by the definition of class-<math id="S7.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> functions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S7.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">VII-C</span> </span><span id="S7.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 ‣ III-C Analysis ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span></h3>

<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the parameter is initialized as <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}=\boldsymbol{\theta}_{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>G</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}=\boldsymbol{\theta}_{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the constraints in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In II-A Problem Formulation ‣ II The Problem ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) holds for any <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies that the initial <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathcal{C}_{\theta,c^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathcal{C}_{\theta,c^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, since <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta}),c^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta}),c^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E18" title="In Lemma 1 ‣ III-B The Proposed Closed-Loop System ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) represents solution satisfying the KKT condition of the QP problem in (<a href="#S3.E17" title="In III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 ‣ III-C Analysis ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> establishes that <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\boldsymbol{\theta})+c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In II-A Problem Formulation ‣ II The Problem ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is a valid CBF, it follows from Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Constraint Satisfaction with CBFs []) ‣ III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that, under the closed-loop dynamics (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), the controller <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{a}(\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In III-A Challenges and Key Ideas ‣ III Main Results ‣ A Control-Barrier-Function-Based Algorithm for Policy Adaptation in Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) guarantees the forward invariance of the constraint-admissible set <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\theta,c^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\theta,c^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we conclude that <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathcal{C}_{\theta,c^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathcal{C}_{\theta,c^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="S7.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
